      "title": "The Art of Memoir",
      "creator": "Mary Karr",
      "note": "I’ve long been fascinated by [Mary Karr](https://twitter.com/marykarrlit), and I originally picked up her book on the craft of memoir writing after a recommendation by [Michael Pollan](https://tim.blog/2019/03/21/michael-pollan-sxsw/?utm_campaign=5bf&utm_medium=convertkit&utm_source=convertkit). It applies to much of life, and I’d consider it a philosophical guide in many respects, replete with the dead serious and spit-up-your-coffee funny. If you work with the written word in any capacity, I highly recommend this read. For more Mary, check out [our conversation on the podcast](https://tim.blog/2020/11/11/mary-karr/?utm_campaign=5bf&utm_medium=convertkit&utm_source=convertkit).",
